      "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith `--engram-config '{\"placement\":\"cpu\",\"replication\":\"per_node\"}'` the engram\nhost table is backed by a memfd. `os.memfd_create` only exists when CPython was\nbuilt against a libc that declares the wrapper; interpreters from conda and from\npython-build-standalone before 20260718 do not, and model construction then dies\nwith:\n\n    File \"sglang/srt/layers/engram.py\", line 751, in _open_shared_fd\n      fd = os.memfd_create(name, 0)\n    AttributeError: module 'os' has no attribute 'memfd_create'\n\n`mem_cache/storage/mmap/mmap_allocator.py`, `layerwise_offload.py` and\n`multimodal_gen/.../utils.py` already guard the same gap; the engram host table\nis the remaining call site without a fallback.\n\n## Modifications\n\n`_memfd_create()` uses `os.memfd_create` when the interpreter has it and issues\nthe same syscall through `libc` otherwise. A `/dev/shm` file is not usable here:\nthese tables are tens of GiB and the container tmpfs is far smaller.\n\n## Not a duplicate\n\nNo open issue or PR changes this call site. #43021 records that uv-managed\npython-build-standalone builds lacked `os.memfd_create`; #44521 (closed) used a\nlibc shim only inside its benchmark harness; #42920 rewrites the engram row-read\npath and does not touch memfd creation.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nN/A - no change to model outputs.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A - startup path only.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `python -m pytest test/registered/unit/layers/test_engram_memfd.py -v`\n  -> 2 passed\n- `python -m pytest test/registered/unit/layers/test_engram_history.py\n  test/registered/unit/layers/test_engram_memfd.py -q` -> 4 passed\n- Simulated a conda CPython (`del os.memfd_create`): the default path falls back\n  to libc and returns a usable descriptor.\n- `pre-commit run --files python/sglang/srt/layers/engram.py\n  test/registered/unit/layers/test_engram_memfd.py` -> all hooks passed\n\nAI assistance was used for this change.\n\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41409251317](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41409251317)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41409251397](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41409251397)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41409251402](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41409251402)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
